<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<WorkflowBuilder Version="2.9.0"
                 xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
                 xmlns:rx="clr-namespace:Bonsai.Reactive;assembly=Bonsai.Core"
                 xmlns:harp="clr-namespace:Bonsai.Harp;assembly=Bonsai.Harp"
                 xmlns:core="clr-namespace:OpenRigs.Core;assembly=OpenRigs.Core"
                 xmlns:dev="clr-namespace:OpenRigs.Devices;assembly=OpenRigs.Devices"
                 xmlns="https://bonsai-rx.org/2018/workflow">
  <Description>The rig's clock from a Behavior board's own Harp clock, for a rig with no timestamp generator; a workflow has exactly one clock. The board is a BehaviorBoard piece, Board. Sets the board's clock to the PC's UTC time, again at each heartbeat until one agrees (SetHarpClock: a write is lost about one start in four), and publishes Timestamp (each heartbeat's time, in Harp seconds) and HarpClockSet (the first Timestamp within 2 s of UTC), announcing HarpClockSet into ReadyStages. HarpClockSet is declared by ReadyGate, which comes before every device: the board's own log waits for it, so a definition here, built from the board's messages, would depend on itself. Without it the board counts from power-on, and every Harp time and file name follows that count (1904). Stops the workflow, naming the board, if its clock is not set within 10 s or its heartbeats stop for 3 s.</Description>
  <Workflow>
    <Nodes>
      <Expression xsi:type="ExternalizedMapping">
        <Property Name="Name" DisplayName="Board" Description="The Behavior board that keeps the rig's time, such as BehaviorBoard-Main." />
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="ExternalizedMapping">
        <Property Name="Name" DisplayName="BoardDataSubjectName" Description="Board.Data: the subject the board's messages are published on." />
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
        <Name />
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
        <Combinator xsi:type="dev:SetHarpClock">
          <dev:Name />
          <dev:ToleranceSeconds>2</dev:ToleranceSeconds>
          <dev:TimeoutSeconds>10</dev:TimeoutSeconds>
          <dev:GapSeconds>3</dev:GapSeconds>
        </Combinator>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="ExternalizedMapping">
        <Property Name="Name" DisplayName="BoardCommandsSubjectName" Description="Board.Commands: the subject the board takes its commands from." />
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="MulticastSubject">
        <Name />
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
        <Name />
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
        <Combinator xsi:type="harp:FilterMessageType">
          <harp:FilterType>Include</harp:FilterType>
          <harp:MessageType>Event</harp:MessageType>
        </Combinator>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="harp:Parse">
        <harp:Register xsi:type="harp:TimestampedTimestampSeconds" />
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="MemberSelector">
        <Selector>Seconds</Selector>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="rx:BehaviorSubject">
        <Name>Timestamp</Name>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
        <Name>Timestamp</Name>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
        <Combinator xsi:type="dev:HarpClockSet">
          <dev:ToleranceSeconds>2</dev:ToleranceSeconds>
        </Combinator>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="MulticastSubject">
        <Name>HarpClockSet</Name>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
        <Combinator xsi:type="core:AnnounceStage">
          <core:Stage>HarpClockSet</core:Stage>
        </Combinator>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="MulticastSubject">
        <Name>ReadyStages</Name>
      </Expression>
    </Nodes>
    <Edges>
      <Edge From="0" To="3" Label="Source2" />
      <Edge From="1" To="2" Label="Source1" />
      <Edge From="1" To="6" Label="Source1" />
      <Edge From="2" To="3" Label="Source1" />
      <Edge From="3" To="5" Label="Source1" />
      <Edge From="4" To="5" Label="Source2" />
      <Edge From="6" To="7" Label="Source1" />
      <Edge From="7" To="8" Label="Source1" />
      <Edge From="8" To="9" Label="Source1" />
      <Edge From="9" To="10" Label="Source1" />
      <Edge From="11" To="12" Label="Source1" />
      <Edge From="12" To="13" Label="Source1" />
      <Edge From="13" To="14" Label="Source1" />
      <Edge From="14" To="15" Label="Source1" />
    </Edges>
  </Workflow>
</WorkflowBuilder>
